id: pm-brief-ce55
title: Adopt --respect-item-release so release attribution matches the rest of the fleet
description: "pm-brief was the only fleet package left out of the fleet-wide --respect-item-release rollout, and its pm-changelog devDependency was still pinned at 2026.7.18. Without the flag, single-window generation ignores an item's release field, so closing a tracker whose fix shipped in an earlier release injects that work into the current window."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: changelog,fleet,release-attribution
created_at: "2026-07-25T01:00:18.208Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T01:00:26.204Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-25T01:00:26.203Z"
author: unknown
acceptance_criteria: "all four pm-changelog invocations in package.json pass --respect-item-release; the pm-changelog devDependency matches the fleet at ^2026.7.24; changelog:check passes with the flag in place; generated CHANGELOG.md output is unchanged"
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T01:00:25.795Z",unknown,"Verified the output is unchanged: with the flag added, changelog:check reports the CHANGELOG is already up to date, so this is a behaviour-preserving adoption for the current item set and only takes effect once an item carries a release field."
close_reason: "All four invocations carry --respect-item-release, devDependency bumped to ^2026.7.24, changelog:check green with output unchanged."
body: ""
